# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large local artefacts. Everything below is either regenerable by the scripts
# in scripts/, or a third-party download. None of it belongs in the history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The cloned WSL distro (~11 GB ext4 image) holding the toolchain, the Python
# virtualenv and the Ollama runtime. The lab installs inside the repository
# folder, which makes this ignore essential rather than optional.
wsl/

# Junctions to the first lab's Ollama binary and GGUF weights, plus any other
# third-party download. Shared rather than duplicated: the weights are ~2 GB.
tools/

# Recorded satellite passes pulled from the SatNOGS archive. Regenerate with
# `make satnogs-fetch`; the observation IDs used are pinned in satnogs/manifest.json
# so the download is reproducible.
satnogs/captures/

# Simulation output: channel time series, KPM stores, run logs, RL checkpoints,
# Vivado project directories. Regenerate with the Makefile targets.
data/
accel/rtl/sim_build/
accel/rtl/vivado/
*.jou
*.log
!eval/figures/*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# CUDA build output
accel/cuda/build/
*.o
*.so

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
